Subject: Use Perl_xsub_ptrtable in XS typemaps and core extensions for Fil-C capabilities
Policy-Class: P4-Audit
Rationale: Adopted and decomposed from pinned Fil-C (cede3de02b42:projects/perl-5.40.0). Standard XS typemaps and core extensions (Encode, Storable, threads, threads::shared, B, DynaLoader, re, Compress::Raw::Zlib) convert C pointers to Perl IVs via PTR2IV/INT2PTR. Routing these conversions through Perl_xsub_ptrtable (zptrtable_encode/zptrtable_decode) preserves Fil-C pointer capabilities across XS boundaries.
Upstream-Status: Fil-C-Specific
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: b14fce6d8d8a

